|~ `::call`, the step that calls a name, and what is declared under it:
   its constructor and the refusals of a call, a name that names
   nothing, a kind that answers no verb of the name, a value given
   modifiers, a value that meets a verb, a value withheld from held code,
   two values a step cannot relate or combine, a call too deep and a
   failure inside a primitive.

   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence]. ~|

:call
  |~~ A call, `add 1`, runs a command: its name finds its verb through
      the kind of the subject, its modifiers are computed against the
      subject, and the verb runs on the subject with their values,
      `10 | add 3` answering `13`.

      In a quote the step is a record, `~(add 1) | first` answering
      `::call{:name :add :modifiers [1]}`: `:name` is the keyword of the
      name it calls and `:modifiers` the step of each modifier, where
      the call gives any. Like every record of a step, its constructor
      holds the rules a step keeps, whether a quote is read from text or
      assembled from data.
      ::link~(::quote | doc) ::link~(::qlang/verbs | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts
        |~~ The record of a command, `:name` and `:modifiers`, built into
            its step.
        ~~|
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ `::call` builds the step of a command from its record, a map;
            a payload of another kind is refused, a map under another tag
            among them.
            ::link~(::call | doc)
        ~~|
    | throws :PayloadNotSchemaError
        |~~ A `::call` is a map of `:name`, a keyword, and `:modifiers`, a
            vector of a word at least, each a literal, a name, a group or a
            tagged literal, and `:field` names the field that does not
            fit: `{:name :take :modifiers [2]} | tag ::call` is the step
            `take 2`, and a call that gives no modifiers holds no
            `:modifiers`.
            ::link~(::call | doc)
        ~~|
    | throws :NameNotCallableError
        |~~ The name of a call is one a step calls, names joined by `/`,
            each a letter or `_` and the letters, digits, `_` and `-` after
            it, the first no word of a literal: `:"a b"` writes two words
            and `:"1"` a number. `:name` holds the name, and `:message`
            what the rule says of it.
            ::link~(::call | doc) ::link~(::qlang/names | doc)
        ~~|
    | carries :NameNotCallableError/message
        |~~ What the rule of a name says of the name. ~~|
        ::string
    | throws :LiteralComputesError
        |~~ A modifier that is a literal computes nothing: the modifier at
            `:index` holds a name or a group, and `:message` writes the
            template `get` builds the shape from, its parts computed
            written as quotes, `get [~(x)]`.
            ::link~(::call | doc) ::link~(::any/get | doc)
        ~~|
    | carries :LiteralComputesError/message
        |~~ What the rule says of the literal, the template `get` builds it
            from.
        ~~|
        ::string
    | throws :HostFailureError
        |~~ A failure inside a primitive: an error of the language the
            runtime is written in escaped a verb, or the primitive a host
            handed beside its source answered
            a value of no kind of the language or threw a refusal whose
            facts hold one, a function, an object of JavaScript, a map whose
            key is no string, a failure whose facts are no map, a value
            under a tag that is no tag, a vector or a map that holds itself,
            or a number past the finite doubles, which is a defect of that
            verb's host; a value the call handed in passes back as it is.
            `:message` carries the host's account of it, or names the call
            and the path where the value of no kind stands in its answer,
            and `:causes` the accounts of the failures beneath it. Its
            trace is that of any error; recovery is a `!|` step, and the
            repair belongs to the host, which declares a refusal of its own
            where it has facts to hand.
            ::link~(::call | doc)
        ~~|
    | carries :HostFailureError/message
        |~~ The host's account of the failure. ~~|
        ::string
    | carries :HostFailureError/causes
        |~~ The accounts of the failures beneath it, outermost first. ~~|
        ::vec
    | throws :ValueTakesNoModifiersError
        |~~ A name the scope binds to a value, and a part the kind of the
            subject wires, take no modifiers: the value is read bare,
            `:five 5 | five`, `card | took`, and `:name` holds the name. A verb of that name the subject does not reach lives
            where `:addresses` names, and a call by its address reaches
            it, `string/five`.
            ::link~(::call | doc)
        ~~|
    | carries :ValueTakesNoModifiersError/name
        |~~ The name, which holds a value and no verb. ~~|
        ::keyword
    | throws :ValueMeetsVerbError
        |~~ A name the scope binds to a value is the name of a verb the
            subject answers, and the step does not choose between them:
            `:count 5 | [1 2] | count` meets `::vec/count`. A name of the
            reader's takes any name a step calls, and meets a verb only where a step
            calls the name on a subject the verb answers,
            `:count 5 | 7 | count` answering `5`; there the verb is called
            by its address, `[1 2] | vec/count`, or the value takes
            another name, `:limit 5`. `:name` holds the name, and
            `:addresses` the verb the subject answers.
            ::link~(::call | doc) ::link~(::bind | doc)
        ~~|
    | carries :ValueMeetsVerbError/name
        |~~ The name, which holds a value and names a verb of the subject.
        ~~|
        ::keyword
    | carries :ValueMeetsVerbError/addresses
        |~~ The address of the verb the subject answers under the name. ~~|
        ::set
    | throws :ValueWithheldError
        |~~ Code held as data, a quote in a name, a field or a page, runs
            in a lane of its own, the verbs of the tree and the names it
            declares itself, and reads no value the reader named: `:name`
            holds the name it read. The quote is written in the step that
            hands it to a verb, `filter ~(gt lim)`, which reads the names
            of that step, the value goes to a function as an input,
            `apply f [4]`, or `fill` writes it into the code.
            ::link~(::call | doc) ::link~(::fn/fill | doc)
        ~~|
    | carries :ValueWithheldError/name
        |~~ The name of the reader's value the held code read. ~~|
        ::keyword
    | carries :ValueTakesNoModifiersError/addresses
        |~~ The addresses where a verb of that name lives, one a
            declaration shadows among them.
        ~~|
        ::set
    | throws :KindAnswersNoVerbError
        |~~ The kind of the subject has no verb of the name while other
            kinds have one: `:name` holds the name, `:actualTag` the kind
            of the subject, and `:addresses` the verbs of the name and the
            kinds they serve, and `:nearest`, where a page leads to one,
            the verbs the pages of those verbs lead to that the subject
            answers and that answer a kind the verbs answer, the act its
            kind keeps under another name, `[1 2] | toString` led to
            `print` and `json`. The subject is turned into one of those
            kinds first, a soft read that answered null given its
            fallback, `query /items | coalesce [] | count`, a keyword its
            name by `toString`, `:host | toString | append ":80"`, or a
            verb of another name was meant, which `:nearest` names where a
            page leads to it. A value under a kind that wires its parts
            answers the verbs of its kind and of every value alone, and no
            verb of the kind of its payload: its parts are read by the
            names its kind wires, which `tag | manifest` lists, `took`.
            ::link~(::call | doc) ::link~(::any/coalesce | doc)
            ::link~(::keyword/toString | doc) ::link~(::kind/wires | doc)
        ~~|
    | carries :KindAnswersNoVerbError/name
        |~~ The name the step called. ~~|
        ::keyword
    | throws :KindsMismatchedError
        |~~ A step met two values it cannot relate or combine:
            `:leftTag` and `:rightTag` name their kinds where their tags
            part, and where a fold met the second, the path of its frame
            names that part. A comparison, `min` and `max` relate two
            values of one kind as `tag` answers it, so a value under a tag
            beside a bare one is a pair of two kinds, related beneath the
            tag by `payload`, `::Width#5 | payload | gt 3`; text that holds
            a number is read by `toNumber`, a container beside a number
            counted first, `count | gte 2`, a value turned by `desc` set
            beside one turned, and a missing value taken out first,
            `filter ~(ne null) | max`, or counted as zero,
            `map ~(coalesce 0) | max`. A step that combines values of one
            kind, `add`, `append`, `concat`, `union` or `sum`, works
            beneath the tags they share, a bare value sharing any,
            `100 | add ::Cents#1` answering `::Cents#101`, so two under
            different tags are brought to one by a word of their reader
            first, `::Dollars#1 | toCents`.
            ::link~(::call | doc) ::link~(::any/gt | doc)
        ~~|
    | throws :UnknownNameError
        |~~ A step called a name nothing declares, no name of the scope
            and no verb of any kind: `:nearest` holds the names it was
            likely meant to be, and `:name` the name as typed. A name is
            declared before the steps that read it, `:x 5 | x`; a field of
            a record is no verb but a key, read by a path, `get /name`;
            and a kind is no verb either: its tag reaches it, which
            `:nearest` names first, `5 | string` pointing to `::string`,
            whose page says how a value becomes text. A name the verbs of
            other kinds answer is refused by
            `::call/KindAnswersNoVerbError`, which names where they live,
            so `:addresses` holds none here.
            ::link~(::call | doc) ::link~(::call/KindAnswersNoVerbError | doc)
            ::link~(::error/nearest | doc)
        ~~|
    | carries :UnknownNameError/name
        |~~ The name the step called. ~~|
        ::keyword
    | throws :UnknownAddressError
        |~~ A name with a path names nothing: no declaration wrote that
            address. `:address` holds the address as a tag name, which the
            axes read, and `:nearest` the addresses it was likely meant to
            be, and `manifest` lists the names a noun holds,
            `::vec | manifest`. An address that names a value reads it, as
            a bare name does.
            ::link~(::call | doc) ::link~(::any/manifest | doc)
        ~~|
    | carries :UnknownAddressError/address
        |~~ The address the step called. ~~|
        ::tag
    | throws :EvaluationDepthExceededError
        |~~ A call too deep: the recipe of a verb, a modifier computed at
            the call, `apply`, a constructor of a tag and each run of the
            code a verb runs, `map ~(…)`, run one deeper in the evaluation
            depth than the step that called them, while the steps of one
            pipeline and a group run at its depth; an input read by its
            selector and a modifier of an atom meet the limit one deeper than
            the call, a quote written as a modifier goes no deeper, and a
            step past the limit refuses, `:depth`
            the evaluation depth refused and `:limit` the deepest one
            evaluation goes. A recursion without a base case, a verb that
            calls itself, is refused here, on the fail track, while the
            host's memory stays bounded: the case that ends the recursion
            is tested first,
            `:number/down ~(if (eq 0) ~(0) ~(sub 1 | down)) | 5 | down`.
            ::link~(::call | doc) ::link~(::any/if | doc)
        ~~|
    | carries :EvaluationDepthExceededError/depth
        |~~ The evaluation depth refused, one past the limit. ~~|
        ::number
    | carries :EvaluationDepthExceededError/limit
        |~~ The limit, the deepest evaluation depth one evaluation goes. ~~|
        ::number
    | proves :holdsTheNameAndTheModifiers
        |~~ A command is a call of its name and its modifiers. ~~|
        ~(~(filter ~(gt 1)) | payload | eq [::call{:name :filter :modifiers [~(gt 1)]}])
    | proves :readsTheName
        |~~ The name of the call is a keyword. ~~|
        ~(~(count) | first | get /name | eq :count)
    | proves :buildsAStep
        |~~ A map under `::call` builds the step. ~~|
        ~({:name :filter :modifiers [~(gt 1)]} | tag ::call | get [~(it)] | tag ::quote | eq ~(filter ~(gt 1)))
    | proves :KindsMismatchedError/refusesTwoTagsInAStep
        |~~ Values under two tags combine in no step, a sum among them, the
            frame naming the part.
        ~~|
        ~(get [~(::Cents#100 | add ::Dollars#1 !| get [~(tag) /leftTag /rightTag]) ~([::Cents#100 ::Dollars#1] | sum !| trace | last | path)]
          | eq [[::call/KindsMismatchedError ::Cents ::Dollars] /1])
    | proves :KindsMismatchedError/laysTheTagABareValueTakes
        |~~ A bare value takes the tag of the other, the answer under it. ~~|
        ~(get [~(::Cents#100 | add 1) ~(100 | add ::Cents#1) ~([1 ::Cents#100] | sum)] | eq [::Cents#101 ::Cents#101 ::Cents#101])
    | proves :KindsMismatchedError/takesAMissingValueOutOfAMaximum
        |~~ `max` relates values of one kind, a missing one taken out first.
        ~~|
        ~(get [~([1 null 3] | max !| tag) ~([1 null 3] | filter ~(ne null) | max)] | eq [::call/KindsMismatchedError 3])
    | proves :KindsMismatchedError/namesTheKindsWhereTheTagsPart
        |~~ The facts name the kinds of the two where their tags part. ~~|
        ~(get [~(::A::T#1 | add ::A::U#2 !| get [/leftTag /rightTag]) ~(::A#1 | add ::A::T#2 !| get [/leftTag /rightTag])]
          | eq [[::T ::U] [::number ::T]])
    | proves :PayloadNotSchemaError/refusesANameThatIsNoKeyword
        |~~ A `:name` that is no keyword is refused, `:field` naming it. ~~|
        ~(::call{:name 42} !| get [~(tag) /field] | eq [::call/PayloadNotSchemaError :name])
    | proves :PayloadNotSchemaError/buildsTheStepOfACall
        |~~ A keyword and a vector of steps build the step of the call. ~~|
        ~({:name :take :modifiers [2]} | tag ::call | get [~(it)] | tag ::quote | eq ~(take 2))
    | proves :PayloadNotSchemaError/refusesAnEmptyVectorOfModifiers
        |~~ An empty vector of modifiers is refused; a call that gives none
            holds no `:modifiers`.
        ~~|
        ~(::call{:name :count :modifiers []}
          !| get [~(tag) /field] | eq [::call/PayloadNotSchemaError :modifiers])
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesAVector
        |~~ A vector is no record of a command. ~~|
        ~(::call[1] !| get [~(tag) /expected] | eq [::call/PayloadKindNotTakenError #[::map]])
    | proves :NameNotCallableError/refusesANameOfTwoWords
        |~~ A name with a space is no name a step calls. ~~|
        ~(::call{:name :"a b"} !| get [~(tag) /name] | eq [::call/NameNotCallableError :"a b"])
    | proves :NameNotCallableError/refusesANameThatReadsAsANumber
        |~~ A name that reads as a number is no name a step calls. ~~|
        ~(::call{:name :"1"} !| tag | eq ::call/NameNotCallableError)
    | proves :NameNotCallableError/refusesTheWordOfALiteral
        |~~ A name whose first word is the word of a literal is no name a
            step calls.
        ~~|
        ~(get [~(::call{:name :null} !| tag) ~(::call{:name :true/count} !| tag)] | eq [::call/NameNotCallableError ::call/NameNotCallableError])
    | proves :LiteralComputesError/refusesANameInsideAModifier
        |~~ A vector of a name given as a modifier computes, and is
            refused.
        ~~|
        ~({:name :take :modifiers [[::call{:name :x}]]} | tag ::call !| get [~(tag) /index] | eq [::call/LiteralComputesError 0])
    | proves :ValueMeetsVerbError/refusesAValueAndAVerbThatMeet
        |~~ A value and a verb that meet at a step are refused with the
            verb's address.
        ~~|
        ~(:count 5 | [1 2] | count !| get [~(tag) /addresses] | eq [::call/ValueMeetsVerbError #[::vec/count]])
    | proves :ValueMeetsVerbError/readsTheValueWhereNoVerbAnswers
        |~~ On a subject no verb of the name answers, the value is read. ~~|
        ~(:count 5 | 7 | count | eq 5)
    | proves :ValueMeetsVerbError/callsTheVerbByItsAddress
        |~~ The verb is called by its address beside the value. ~~|
        ~(:count 5 | [1 2] | vec/count | eq 2)
    | proves :ValueMeetsVerbError/meetsTheVerbOfAFold
        |~~ A value named as the verb of a fold meets it there, and the
            address calls the verb.
        ~~|
        ~(:add 5 | [1 2 3] | get [~(reduce 0 ~(add) !| tag) ~(reduce 0 ~(number/add))] | eq [::call/ValueMeetsVerbError 6])
    | proves :ValueMeetsVerbError/meetsAnInputInTheRecipeOfAVerb
        |~~ An input named as a verb meets the verb in the recipe that
            reads it.
        ~~|
        ~(:vec/firstN (::fn | takes :count |~~ How many. ~~| /0 | impl ~(get [~(count) ~(take count)])) | [1 2 3] | firstN 2 !| get [~(tag) /name] | eq [::call/ValueMeetsVerbError :count])
    | proves :ValueTakesNoModifiersError/refusesModifiersOnAValue
        |~~ A name that holds a value refuses the modifiers a call gives
            it.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | :five it | five 42
          !| get [~(tag) /name /actualTag] | eq [::call/ValueTakesNoModifiersError :five ::number])
    | proves :ValueTakesNoModifiersError/namesWhereAVerbOfTheNameLives
        |~~ The refusal names where a verb of the name lives that the
            subject does not reach.
        ~~|
        ~(:five 5 | :string/five ~(1) | 3 | five 42 !| get [~(tag) /addresses] | eq [::call/ValueTakesNoModifiersError #[::string/five]])
    | proves :ValueTakesNoModifiersError/reachesTheVerbByItsAddress
        |~~ A call by its address reaches the verb of the name. ~~|
        ~(:five 5 | :string/five ~(1) | "s" | string/five | eq 1)
    | proves :KindAnswersNoVerbError/namesTheKindAndTheVerbs
        |~~ The refusal names the kind of the subject and where the verbs
            of the name live.
        ~~|
        ~(1 | count !| get [/actualTag ~(get /addresses | has ::vec/count)] | eq [::number true])
    | proves :KindAnswersNoVerbError/namesTheRepairOfAPath
        |~~ A name called on a path names the repair, the step the call was
            likely meant as.
        ~~|
        ~(/tags | count !| get /repair | eq ~(get /tags | count))
    | proves :KindAnswersNoVerbError/listsEveryKindTheNameServes
        |~~ `:addresses` lists every kind the name serves. ~~|
        ~(5 | count
          !| get [~(tag) /addresses]
          |  eq [::call/KindAnswersNoVerbError #[::map/count ::string/count ::vec/count]])
    | proves :KindAnswersNoVerbError/namesTheVerbsOfAReadersNouns
        |~~ The verbs of the name under a reader's nouns are named by
            their addresses.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~| | :Ring |~~ A ring. ~~|
          | :Box/area ~(1) | :Ring/area ~(2)
          | 5 | area
          !| get [~(tag) /addresses]
          |  eq [::call/KindAnswersNoVerbError #[::Box/area ::Ring/area]])
    | proves :KindAnswersNoVerbError/namesTheVerbsItsPagesLeadTo
        |~~ `:nearest` names the verbs the pages of the verbs lead to that
            the subject answers.
        ~~|
        ~({:a 1} | toVec !| get /nearest | eq [:entries :vals])
    | proves :KindAnswersNoVerbError/turnsTheSubjectFirst
        |~~ A soft read that answered null is given its fallback first. ~~|
        ~({} | query /items | coalesce [] | count | eq 0)
    | proves :KindAnswersNoVerbError/turnsAKeywordIntoItsName
        |~~ A keyword turned into its name takes the verbs of strings. ~~|
        ~(:host | toString | append ":80" | eq "host:80")
    | proves :UnknownNameError/refusesANameNothingDeclares
        |~~ A name nothing declares is refused, with no addresses. ~~|
        ~(thisIsNotDefined !| get [~(tag) /addresses] | eq [::call/UnknownNameError #[]])
    | proves :UnknownNameError/suggestsTheNearestName
        |~~ The names nearest in spelling are suggested. ~~|
        ~(fist !| get /nearest | eq [:first])
    | proves :UnknownNameError/suggestsTheReadersNames
        |~~ A reader's own names are suggested too. ~~|
        ~(:limit 3 | limti !| get /nearest | eq [:limit])
    | proves :UnknownNameError/suggestsAVerbThePageOfItsBeginningLinks
        |~~ A name that goes on past a verb is led where the page of that
            verb links.
        ~~|
        ~({:x 1} | addOf (get /x) (get /x) !| get /nearest | eq [:add :sumOf])
    | proves :UnknownNameError/suggestsNothingFarAway
        |~~ A name near nothing suggests nothing. ~~|
        ~(zzzzqqq !| get /nearest | eq [])
    | proves :UnknownNameError/refusesANameReadBeforeItsDeclaration
        |~~ A name read before its declaration names nothing yet. ~~|
        ~(x | :x 5 !| tag | eq ::call/UnknownNameError)
    | proves :UnknownNameError/pointsAKindToItsTag
        |~~ The name of a kind points to its tag. ~~|
        ~(5 | string !| get [~(tag) /nearest] | eq [::call/UnknownNameError [::string]])
    | proves :UnknownNameError/readsNoFieldAsAVerb
        |~~ A field of a record called as a verb names nothing. ~~|
        ~(~(take 2) | first | modifiers !| get [~(tag) /name] | eq [::call/UnknownNameError :modifiers])
    | proves :UnknownAddressError/refusesAnAddressNothingDeclares
        |~~ An address no declaration wrote is refused. ~~|
        ~([1 2 3] | vec/nothing !| get [~(tag) /address] | eq [::call/UnknownAddressError ::vec/nothing])
    | proves :UnknownAddressError/suggestsTheNearestAddress
        |~~ The addresses nearest in spelling are suggested. ~~|
        ~([1] | vec/countt !| get /nearest | has ::vec/count)
    | proves :UnknownAddressError/readsAValueByItsAddress
        |~~ A value under a label is read by its address. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~| | :Box/side 3 | Box/side | eq 3)
    | proves :ValueWithheldError/refusesAValueOfTheReader
        |~~ A quote held in a name reads no value of the reader. ~~|
        ~(:big ~(gt lim) | :lim 4 | [1 5 10] | filter big !| get [~(tag) /name] | eq [::call/ValueWithheldError :lim])
    | proves :EvaluationDepthExceededError/refusesARunawayRecursion
        |~~ A verb that calls itself without end is refused past the
            limit of the evaluation depth.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/inf ~(add 1 | inf) | 0 | inf !| tag | eq ::call/EvaluationDepthExceededError)
    | proves :EvaluationDepthExceededError/namesADepthPastTheLimit
        |~~ The depth refused lies past the limit. ~~|
        ~(:any/q ~(q) | q !| :e it | get /depth | gt (e | get /limit))
    | proves :EvaluationDepthExceededError/endsARecursionByItsBaseCase
        |~~ A recursion that tests its base case first ends. ~~|
        ~(:number/down ~(if (eq 0) ~(0) ~(sub 1 | down)) | 5 | down | eq 0)
    | impl ::builtin{}

